    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d696-a3">

                <pb facs="0693" n="577" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg577"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3—Translation.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister for Foreign Affairs to Ambassador
                    Page</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ministry for Foreign Affairs</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Rome</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-08-27">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 27, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Ambassador</hi>: Referring to my note of the 23d
                        instant<anchor n="12" xml:id="d696-f1"/> concerning the case of Da Prato, I
                    have the honor to inform your excellency relative to Francesco Ghiloni and Leroy
                    Barsotti both of whom were born Italian citizens whose fathers were Italian and
                    who became Americans only in their minority by naturalization of their fathers,
                    the Royal Ministry of War confirms its previous decision and has declared its
                    inability to permit their release.</p>
                <p>I must therefore confirm to your excellency the communication already made in my
                    note of May 16 and note of July 19 concerning the above-mentioned youths.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">S. Sonnino.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d696-f1" n="12" xml:id="d696-f1-content">
                <p>The inclosure with Mr. Page’s No. 360 of August 24.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
